{"kind":"assert","text":"Required archive660 protocol Source finding at07b066ab8f850598e3ba06dcbcaad8e2d5302d52: non-binary pkt-lines incorrectly require a trailing LF. The new v2Capabilities compares the version packet to \"version 2\\n\" and rejects every capability whose final byte is not LF. v2Pack likewise requires LF in shallow-info/packfile section headers and the exact shallow boundary. Git's common pkt-line rule requires receivers to treat non-binary payloads equivalently with or without one trailing LF: https://git-scm.com/docs/gitprotocol-common#_pkt_line_format . The existing v0 readPacket already implements that convention. The candidate therefore refuses conforming v2 replies even if all section, object and capability identities are correct.\n\nThe original real local Git v2 witness failed at isolated shallow boundary (b797b87a). Missing LF is a concrete Source/specification defect and a hypothesis for that recorded failure; I have not yet read its actual response bytes, so I do not assert the runtime cause. Correct only the non-binary framing boundary: treat at most the optional final LF equivalently before the same exact version, capability, section and requested-object checks. Keep binary sideband payloads byte-for-byte, plus all packet/byte/deadline/count/hash/type bounds, no-extra-section/no-trailing-data rules and no fallback. Do not relax object identity, accept CR/embedded controls or trim arbitrary whitespace.\n\nExtend the bounded existing v2 framing/capability witness to cover LF-present and LF-absent non-binary version/capability/header/shallow packets, preserving malformed/duplicate/foreign/extra-section controls and the real local Git exchange. The healthy deadline witnesses remain their actual outcomes; required9ef is Source-resolved. This new issue qualifies the broader no-further-required-Source-finding assessment in bf2, rather than reopening the deadline correction. Urgent Growad99 remains first priority. Only affected local checks and the still-owed final exact-head gate are needed after correction; no checker runtime or blanket healthy repeat is requested."}